{"kind":"request","text":"R3a: throwaway keys must not lock newcomers out of a room\n\nR3 (landed f1f6a8b9, deployed 13:53) bounds each remote authority run at 4,096 distinct signing keys and answers `limit` to a new key above that. The checker found (5b0fcc38) that failed and once-only reads count toward the bound. A caller who can send well-formed signed acts can fill all 4,096 places with throwaway keys. Every later new key in that run then gets `limit`, including a member who has just joined. Joining is a core path, so this is a defect in the bound I chose in 03e5f6d7, not an accepted residual.\n\nInvariant: in one run, after any number of acts from keys that Membership gives no standing, a member's key, including one that joined during the run, is still admitted. The memory that the run keeps for reads stays bounded.\n\nDirection: keep the counted bound for keys that Membership grants standing. Hold denied reads outside that count, either not kept or in a separate bounded store that drops its oldest entry instead of refusing. If run consistency requires a denied or once-only read to stay kept, name the invariant that requires it and propose before any source edit.\n\nWork:\n1. Read-only source map and proposal first: where the bound counts keys, what a once-only read is, and which choice keeps the R3 turn order intact. Report it to the planner before any source edit.\n2. Witness: one run takes acts from more than 4,096 throwaway keys, then a newly joined member's act is admitted; the kept-read memory stays within its bound. One control: restore today's counting and show the witness fails with `limit`.\n3. Update the residual paragraph in docs/security/threat-model.md (\"Trust assumptions and residual exposure\") to state what remains after the fix.\n\nIf the proposal shows the fix is larger than a phase 1 item, land the threat-model sentence alone as a docs-only change that names the exhaustion residual, and bring the fix back to me for placement.\n\nOrder: phase 1, a parallel lane beside BR-14. Step 1 can start now. Its gate waits for the local slot; one gate at a time on the machine. Common conditions as in 954bf397: checker review of the exact head before landing, one gate at the final head, and the planner deploys all four Workers after landing.","body":{"conditions":"Throwaway keys cannot make a member's key, including one that joined in the run, get limit; kept-read memory stays bounded; proposal before source edit; witness plus one control; threat-model residual updated.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}